			</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19104021">
			</marker>
			<v n="21">
				The young 
				<crossref let="p" cid="c19104021.41">
				</crossref>
				lions roar, 
				<crossref let="q" cid="c19104021.42">
				</crossref>
				for their prey, seeking their food from God.
				<note nid="n19104021.21">
				</note>
			</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19104022">
			</marker>
			<v n="22">
				When the 
				<crossref let="r" cid="c19104022.43">
				</crossref>
				sun rises,, 
				<crossref let="s" cid="c19104022.44">
				</crossref>
				they steal away and lie down in their dens.
			</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19104023">
			</marker>
			<v n="23">
				Man goes 
				<crossref let="t" cid="c19104023.45">
				</crossref>
				out to, 
				<crossref let="u" cid="c19104023.46">
				</crossref>
				his work and to his labor until the evening.
			</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19104024">
			</marker>
			<v n="24">
				O LORD, 
				<crossref let="v" cid="c19104024.47">
				</crossref>
				how manifold, 
				<crossref let="w" cid="c19104024.48">
				</crossref>
				are your works! In wisdom have you made them all; the earth is full of your creatures.
				<note nid="n19104024.24">
				</note>
			</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19104025">
			</marker>
			<v n="25">
				Here is 
				<crossref let="x" cid="c19104025.49">
				</crossref>
				the sea,, 
				<crossref let="y" cid="c19104025.50">
				</crossref>
				great and wide, which teems with creatures innumerable, living things both small and great.
			</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19104026">
			</marker>
			<v n="26">
				There go 
				<crossref let="z" cid="c19104026.51">
				</crossref>
				the ships,, 
				<crossref let="a" cid="c19104026.52">
				</crossref>
				and Leviathan, which you formed to play in it.(2)
			</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19104027">
			</marker>
			<v n="27">
				These all 
				<crossref let="b" cid="c19104027.53">
				</crossref>
				look to, 
				<crossref let="c" cid="c19104027.54">
				</crossref>
				you, to give them their food in due season.
				<note nid="n19104027.27">
				</note>
			</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19104028">
			</marker>
			<v n="28">
				When you 
				<crossref let="d" cid="c19104028.55">
				</crossref>
				give it, 
				<crossref let="e" cid="c19104028.56">
				</crossref>
				to them, they gather it up; when you open your hand, they are filled with good things.
			</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19104029">
			</marker>
			<v n="29">
				When you 
				<crossref let="f" cid="c19104029.57">
				</crossref>
